Subject: DEBUG: trace who renders the screen bar, and when

Not applied by default -- the filename has no number, so setup.sh's
[0-9]*.patch glob skips it. Apply it by hand when the question below comes up
again.

The question it answers is ISSUE-0043's open one. The boot splash holds the
display until the desktop is drawn, and the screen title bar arrives about
100 ms after the release signal, drawn by something that has not been
identified. CreateScreenBar() is ruled out: it runs at screen creation, before
Show(), and therefore before the hold begins. RenderScreenBar() is reached only
from there, from ActivateWindow() and from the input handler -- and the last
two queue through DoASyncAction(), whose queue is drained by the input handler,
which a boot with no input never runs.

Something draws it anyway. These two files are where the evidence is:

  intuition_misc.c        RenderScreenBar() already carries D(bug(...)), so
                          every call announces itself
  inputhandler_actions.c  HandleIntuiActions() and int_showtitle(), so the
                          queue draining is visible too

Read against the BootUI timestamps -- "hold armed", "hold released",
"display takeover" -- that places every render on the same timeline as the
hold, which is what the question needs.

Verbose. This is a bring-up aid, not a setting.
---
--- a/rom/intuition/intuition_misc.c
+++ b/rom/intuition/intuition_misc.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 
 
 #undef DEBUG
-#define DEBUG 0
+#define DEBUG 1
 #   include <aros/debug.h>
 
 ULONG addextragadget(struct Window *w,BOOL is_gzz,struct DrawInfo *dri,LONG relright,ULONG imagetype,ULONG gadgetid,ULONG gadgettype,struct IntuitionBase *IntuitionBase);
--- a/rom/intuition/inputhandler_actions.c
+++ b/rom/intuition/inputhandler_actions.c
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 #include "menus.h"
 
 #undef DEBUG
-#define DEBUG 0
+#define DEBUG 1
 #include <aros/debug.h>
 
 #define LOCK_ACTIONS()      ObtainSemaphore(&GetPrivIBase(IntuitionBase)->IntuiActionLock);
